# Wave: v0.10.5-legacy-decisions W9
# Covers: waituntil (e?) — blocks strand until e fires; payload delivered.
#         Ruling: implemented (Wave 6 W9, legacy F4).
#
# Semantics: `waituntil (e?)` parks the calling strand on e's waiters_head
#   via c_event_waituntil.  When e is emitted, the emit payload is deposited
#   in strand->last_event_payload; on resume, urbi_vm_dispatch_loop_until_yield
#   delivers the payload to the OP_CALL result register before the first
#   instruction executes.  The expression evaluates to the emit payload.
#
# Test layout: a tag-prefixed block runs concurrently and blocks on
#   waituntil(e?); the main thread fires e!(99); Realm.got is then 99.
#
# Note: single-line form required; REPL processes one line at a time.
#
# Activated: 2026-05-26 as part of v0.10.5-legacy-decisions W9.

var e = Event.new()
var got = 0
var myTag = Tag.new()
myTag: { Realm.got = waituntil(e?) }
e!(99)
Realm.got
[00000000] <event>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 99
